{
  "version": 1,
  "mode": "behavior",
  "reason": "Protects the touchbard entry path for the opt-in device run: --drm/--touch parse only as opt-in flags and never with the simulator window; a path that is not a /dev/dri/cardN or /dev/input/eventN node is refused before sysfs or the input devices are read; the card is identified in sysfs before it is opened and its opened node confirmed before master; a refused start or digitizer shows nothing and releases the card; each tap acts once; cancel, lost sync, read errors, daemon errors, unplug (Gone) and a failed restore are reported and restore exactly once; a stop signal ends a run with a blocked reader promptly with one restore; commands keep the caller's signal mask; the simulator's flags, frames and default signal actions are unchanged. Every touchbard a TB-47 test starts, as a process (touchbard_hardware) or in-process (--bin touchbard and its test-binary children), keeps its generation store out of the caller's XDG_STATE_HOME: the xdg-decoy check runs each path against its own decoy, requires it unchanged and fails closed when a path proves too little; on request the signal test itself requires each HUP/INT/TERM round to keep one absent first-write generation in that round's own HOME (integration amendment at 987a398, see .scratch/TB-47/qa-integration-isolation/RECEIPT.md).",
